`saveTodo()` always includes `description` in the update payload (even when the user clears it to an empty string). The backend `UpdateTodo` handler currently only applies description updates when the value is non-empty, so users cannot clear an existing description and will see it “reappear” after saving. Consider adjusting the API contract to support explicit clearing (e.g., make `description` a nullable/pointer field or include a separate “field present” indicator), or update the UI to disallow/communicate that descriptions can’t be cleared until the backend supports it.

